{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>STM.SpecDefaults</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"qcheck-stm","href":"../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"STM","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"SpecDefaults","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>Default implementations for state machine specifications that can be given useful defaults.</p><p>The intention is that extended spec modules would <code>include</code> the defaults:</p><pre class=\"language-ocaml\"><code>  module MySpec = struct\u000A    include SpecDefaults\u000A\u000A    (* ... *)\u000A  end</code></pre><p>This way the spec module can usually just continue working after new specifications have been added to <a href=\"../module-type-SpecExt/index.html\"><code>SpecExt</code></a> with defaults in <a href=\"#\"><code>SpecDefaults</code></a>.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-cleanup\"><a href=\"#val-cleanup\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> cleanup : <span><span class=\"type-var\">'sut</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>cleanup sut</code> just returns <code>()</code>.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-precond\"><a href=\"#val-precond\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> precond : <span><span class=\"type-var\">'cmd</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"type-var\">'state</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> bool</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>precond cmd state</code> just returns <code>true</code>.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-wrap_cmd_seq\"><a href=\"#val-wrap_cmd_seq\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> wrap_cmd_seq : <span><span>(<span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>)</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>wrap_cmd_seq thunk</code> is equivalent to <code>thunk ()</code>.</p></div></div>"}